  {
   "id": "concept2",
   "type": "concept",
   "title": {
    "en": "Substitution in definite integrals"
   },
   "body": {
    "en": "When you put $t = g(x)$, change the limits too: $x = a$ becomes $t = g(a)$ and $x = b$ becomes $t = g(b)$. Then there is no need to go back to $x$.",
    "kn": "t = g(x) ಆದೇಶಿಸಿದಾಗ ಮಿತಿಗಳನ್ನೂ ಬದಲಿಸಿ: x = a ⇒ t = g(a), x = b ⇒ t = g(b). ಮತ್ತೆ x ಗೆ ಹಿಂದಿರುಗಬೇಕಿಲ್ಲ."
   },
   "points": [
    {
     "en": "New limits: g(a) and g(b)"
    },
    {
     "en": "No need to substitute back"
    }
   ],
   "narration": {
    "en": "When you substitute in a definite integral, change the limits as well. Then you never need to return to x.",
    "kn": "t = g(x) ಆದೇಶಿಸಿದಾಗ ಮಿತಿಗಳನ್ನೂ ಬದಲಿಸಿ: x = a ⇒ t = g(a), x = b ⇒ t = g(b). ಮತ್ತೆ x ಗೆ ಹಿಂದಿರುಗಬೇಕಿಲ್ಲ."
   }
  },
